course: dictionary
lesson: 8663
title: Sec: a very short time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sec is an informal word, short for second. In everyday talk, «Hang on a sec» and «Back in a sec» mean wait a very short time. Nobody is counting exactly one second when they say it.
explain: Be careful, because a sec is not always a real time. «Two secs», «one sec» and «in a minute» all mean soon. Soon can be 10 minutes, which is 600 seconds, so the clue is the situation, not the number.
explain: In writing about timing, sec is an abbreviation with an exact value. «She ran 100 m in 15 sec» means 15 seconds, precisely. Context tells you which kind of sec you are reading: a casual chat or an exact measurement.
fact: Sec is short for second, a unit of time.
fact: «Wait a sec» means wait a very short time. It is informal, so you hear it in speech more than you see it in formal writing.
fact: «15 sec» in a race report means exactly 15 seconds.
fact: There are 60 seconds in a minute, so 10 minutes is 600 seconds.
fact: Sec can also be short for secretary, or for secant in maths.
exercise: «Hang on a sec, I'm nearly ready.» What does a sec mean here? | Exactly 60 minutes | *A very short time | A type of cup | A kind of dance
exercise: «She ran 100 m in 15 sec.» What does sec stand for? | secant | *second | minute | secretary
exercise: Ben says «two secs» means exactly two seconds. Is he right? | *No, it is a vague phrase that means soon, not a real time | No, it means two hours | Yes, because it has a number in it | Yes, it is exactly two seconds
test: «I'll be there in a minute», Mum says, and it takes 20 minutes. What does in a minute mean here? | Right now, at once | Never | *Soon, which can be quite a while | Exactly one minute
test: In an office note, «the sec typed the letter» means the typed letter came from which job? | *secretary | secant | a dog | second
exam: «Two secs», «one sec» and «in a minute» are not real times. What do they all mean? | Exactly ten minutes | Never | Exactly one second | *Soon, which can be a long wait
